#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:5
#: 4f2aba8bc36845419eb6e9af9fb36ef9
msgid "Tuning Steering and navigation for a Rover (ver 3.1 and older)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:7
#: 103de7ba16a54074840619aa8cb6b923
msgid "**ARCHIVED**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:11
#: ccba27f6148143dca3d16dc725abca01
msgid "These instructions are relevant for Rover-3.1 and older. For newer versions of the Rover firmware please refer to these :ref:`steering <rover-tuning-steering-rate>` and :ref:`navigation tuning guides <rover-tuning-navigation>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:15
#: 0bc1f32628914897b815f27bf0566394
msgid "When setting up a Rover there are 6 key parameters you need to get right. This guide provides a set of steps to get those parameters right, so that your rover will accurately navigate in AUTO mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:20
#: 16ad4bb266fa4d40977e2771ec2d4f20
msgid "The key parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:22
#: 1a6026a065d542df94570b80cf261f6b
msgid "``STEER2SRV_P``: This tells the rover code what the turning circle (as a diameter in meters) is for your rover. It is critical that you get this parameter right, as it tells the code what steering angle to choose to achieve a desired turn rate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:26
#: 594787de731248f480e0b9d316920e4e
msgid "``TURN_MAX_G``: This tells the rover the maximum G force (in multiples of one gravity) that your rover can handle while remaining stable. If you set this too high then your rover may flip over in turns, or skid. If you set it too low then your rover will not be able to turn sharply enough."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:31
#: ff388d0035dd4b25b84777d914cd10c0
msgid "``NAVL1_PERIOD``: This controls the aggressiveness of the navigation algorithm. A smaller number means more aggressive turning in AUTO mode, a large number means larger, smoother turns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:34
#: a44b4bd0e69a44c59437b0b4cb9c1970
msgid "``SPEED_TURN_GAIN``: This controls how much the rover should slow down while turning, as a percentage of current target speed. To not slow down at all in turns set this to 100. When doing initial tuning it is recommended you use 100, and lower this later to improve handling of tight courses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:39
#: 0780cb87ea074d0f959b251736a82618
msgid "``CRUISE_SPEED``: This controls the target speed in meters/second in AUTO."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:41
#: 061f9b67e2084519afd2cd708224ed50
msgid "``CRUISE_THROTTLE``: This sets the initial guess at what throttle is needed to achieve CRUISE_SPEED when driving straight ahead. This needs to be **RIGHT** for the rover to achieve good speed control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:46
#: 4f8646604e1e43c08454015edfeb7b2f
msgid "Step 1: Setting initial parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:48
#: 9a0e3b6377b64dfea5e4b3dfdd4a49a7
msgid "To start the tuning process set the following values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:50
#: 4680ec5e045443c4b560a72bf3168272
msgid "STEER2SRV_P = 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:51
#: 6ed86364e3584799bf827157343d23c6
msgid "TURN_MAX_G = 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:52
#: a311453b6e0c4c73a4c7f0b3806b98e5
msgid "NAVL1_PERIOD = 6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:53
#: cb0cd2f87bd8447cb010ad9b00c51e40
msgid "SPEED_TURN_GAIN = 100"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:54
#: 612fa1ac07b3439b911f834b71e1951c
msgid "CRUISE_SPEED = 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:55
#: 3a1a9d8badea443eb8e31241d53d1ff7
msgid "CRUISE_THROTTLE = 20"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:57
#: 78ff87333a0f4037b556fcce84928110
msgid "These are conservative values that should give you slow, gentle behaviour for most rovers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:61
#: 18675cd7b9fe40cdb5ca6f824190b99d
msgid "Step 2: Setting CRUISE_THROTTLE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:63
#: f7bcda7f2cab428e93e36bff5eadd01b
msgid "We need to get ``CRUISE_THROTTLE`` right so we know what throttle level will give us a speed of 2 meters/second."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:66
#: 957c616c4c2042bb96cc4236c7beac7b
msgid "Switch to MANUAL mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:67
#: 59e3a9c277be47998f1a24d4bb542c48
msgid "Slowly advance the throttle until the ground station shows a speed of 2 meters/second"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:69
#: c940fdea76884fc6b0c3e528300cbf2a
msgid "note the throttle percentage shown in the HUD"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:70
#: 315c89f11ac3470691fbb1e073f81b37
msgid "set CRUISE_THROTTLE to the percentage needed for straight driving at 2 meters/second"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:74
#: 1eaf95ed5674439385686b638223d686
msgid "Step 3: Setting the STEER2SRV_P"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:76
#: a73c94b09f444071ac8d28a012df8ee4
msgid "To set your STEER2SRV_P parameter you need to measure the diameter of the turning circle of your rover."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:79
#: d4c4b86e01f044d9af92bea2956f08ef
msgid "Put your rover into MANUAL mode, and put the steering hard over to one side. Then very slowly drive your rover in a circle. Use a tape measure to measure the diameter of that circle and set STEER2SRV_P to that value in meters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:85
#: 278697783b54459482fcd3d84c82be87
msgid "Step 4: tuning TURN_MAX_G"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:87
#: b28d09d438364cee82ae43228edf47d9
msgid "The ``TURN_MAX_G`` parameter can now be tuned so that your rover can drive more aggressively, without turning over."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:90
#: ef5d96e05d66429c987f461ac5b1b347
msgid "put into STEERING mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:91
#: 3587e57e7f104ad2b3a48fe9186d4f48
msgid "turn at maximum turn rate and maximum throttle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:92
#: 6632d2a662d64ad6b0c6ec3489eabd7d
msgid "adjust TURN_MAX_G to highest level that rover remains stable, doesn't start to roll over and doesn't skid"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:96
#: c7403ed81d9e478dafb2282cd828b966
msgid "Step 5: tuning NAVL1_PERIOD"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:98
#: aadb75addb3f4de0bcddd5d8027e119b
msgid "Now you can finally start tuning your steering in AUTO mode. To tune in AUTO you will need to create a mission for your rover to navigate. A simple rectangular mission is the best to start with."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:102
#: bb71dc29c980483d9c30f42bc9528ea4
msgid "create a rectangular course for the rover"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:103
#: f416450b05fa461686b427323f4a351a
msgid "run the course in AUTO mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:104
#: 563297376a5f4d3097957888231c9367
msgid "if the rover weaves along the straights, then raise NAVL1_PERIOD in increments of 0.5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:106
#: 7d5f28b1fe1b4ed5ad221f6caa577dee
msgid "if the rover doesn't turn sharply enough then lower NAVL1_PERIOD in increments of 0.5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:108
#: e21ed99c69534bba84047f82a134cf7d
msgid "if the rover is turning too late in corners then raise WP_RADIUS in increments of 1.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:111
#: f7e15d631fdc4027886d974e39583972
msgid "You may also find that you may need to raise NAVL1_DAMPING slightly to improve navigation in tight courses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:115
#: cb824433de25481081a4692fa02e3001
msgid "Final Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:117
#: a833687b505f413d9f678a1003356489
msgid "Now that you have the basic parameters tuned you may find you can go back and raise CRUISE_SPEED for faster driving. If you do, then make sure you adjust CRUISE_THROTTLE to suit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:121
#: 04277fb204fa4959b94b7167677871e9
msgid "You may also like to lower SPEED_TURN_GAIN to ask the rover to slow down a bit when turning. That would allow for higher speeds when driving straight ahead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:125
#: 6819aa1f1e6648e28ac1f045cdd520da
msgid "There are a number of other parameters that can be used to fine tune your steering once you have completed the basic ones above. Please see the :doc:`full parameter list <parameters>` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:129
#: bf115a9e9c0941d2a47905de83477cdf
msgid "Some parameters to pay particular attention to are STEER2SRV_TCONST, STEER2SRV_I, STEER2SRV_D and STEER2SRV_IMAX."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:133
#: c80179fb980f468781f33edc8a2454e2
msgid "Fixing problems with weaving"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:135
#: f65dcba5ab3443abae53bd5f7470f96c
msgid "A common issue with rovers is that the steering 'weaves', turning from side to side rather than turning smoothly. There can be several possible reasons for this happening."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:139
#: 97c147cc413348d5a4344eb083d1096c
msgid "The first thing you need to work out is if the problem is confined to low speed driving or also affects higher speed driving. If the problem only happens at very low speed (such as when first entering auto on a mission) then the most likely problem is that STEER2SRV_MINSPD is too low. The default is 1.0 m/s, which is quite low, and if your GPS heading isn't very reliable at low speed then you may need to raise that number. Try 2.0 and see if that helps with low speed weaving."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:147
#: 1e3ed1bf14064baca8e2e23ce0f6ae2d
msgid "If the problem also happens at higher speeds then it is likely to either be the L1 navigation tuning or the steering controller tuning. To fix it you will need to understand how these parameters work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:151
#: 8ddb930d387648b4bad3f121d5ccf526
msgid "The NAVL1_PERIOD controls how rapidly the L1 navigation controller changes the demanded steering direction. Making this number larger will reduce weaving in AUTO, but it will also mean that you can't steer as accurately around tight corners. Try raising NAVL1_PERIOD in steps of 0.5 until the weaving stops. For most rovers a value between 6.0 and 8.0 is good, but some rovers may need higher values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:158
#: 1c6e2da2ed9c4196943663478677249d
msgid "If raising the NAVL1_PERIOD fixes the weaving but leaves you unable to handle sharp turns in missions then you will instead need to tune the steering controller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:162
#: 8d07fe02a31e4dccb800ad71ec5e3248
msgid "In the steering controller there are 3 key parameters that will control weaving:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:165
#: fb17e4492f334d959044a7b1e539acfe
msgid "A smaller STEER2SRV_P will reduce weaving, try reducing it by 0.1 at a time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:167
#: 24177ea55d81415b845a6608e0e7e76f
msgid "A larger STEER2SRV_D will \"damp\" the weaving, but if you make it too large then you will get high speed oscillation. For example you may find that a value of 0.1 reduces the damping, but a value of 0.2 could cause a high speed oscillation in the steering servo. If you get fast oscillation then reduce the STEER2SRV_D value by 50%."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:172
#: 2ce40d4e710f442da69a137c27954333
msgid "A larger STEER2SRV_TCONST will slow down the steering controller, which will reduce weaving. Try raising it in steps of 0.1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/tuning-steering-and-navigation-for-a-rover.rst:175
#: 393fdc27ac074e979cc239c77e985303
msgid "With the current controller system you do need to experiment a bit with these values to get the behaviour you want. We hope to introduce an automatic tuning system in future, but for now manual tuning is needed."
msgstr ""
